# Build DayQ Energy and Industry Progression

Read [FULL_CONTRACT.md](references/FULL_CONTRACT.md) and [INTEGRATION.md](references/INTEGRATION.md).

The energy/industrial progression is `decided` by the user. Exact rates, yields, timings, capacities, power values, and loot frequencies remain testing variables; do not use balance work to reopen the approved gameplay direction.

Resolve the DayQ workspace root from `DAYQ_ROOT` or the nearest current-directory ancestor containing `dayq/references` and `dayq/skills`. Read the complete locked source at `$DAYQ_ROOT/dayq/references/DAYQ_ENERGY_INDUSTRY_PROGRESSION_LOCKED_SOURCE.md`; stop if it is unavailable. Reject these superseded designs:

- Manual Camp -> Mechanized War Economy as the defining eight-stage abstraction;
- the disconnected capability-web proposal;
- ordinary twenty-eight-year-old gasoline as usable loot;
- F1 forge becoming an industrial foundry through a menu upgrade;
- new hydrogen cylinders before restored heavy industry;
- electrolysis or hydrogen as the normal base-energy bootstrap;
- certificate hunts, test-item hunts, chemistry chores, or arbitrary Stirling component tokens.

The mandatory proof route is:

`dead battery sources -> donor extraction -> empty B0 at Field Battery Bench -> earned first charge -> Edge agent -> restored P1 and concise F1 forge -> donor adaptation -> LS0 and compact plastic converter -> burner oil -> LS0 operation -> B1 charge -> sustained workshop`

Preserve the existing inventory, crafting/job, manufacturing-gate, power, fire, building, progression, persistence, and multiplayer owners. Passing quarantined RF0-RF5 tests prove reusable transaction mechanics only and never progression acceptance.
